# Soulcoil Viper: "target creature card from your graveyard". Bot2's own Bolt kills its own Memnite on turn 2, so a creature card sits in
# Bot2's graveyard and none in Bot1's: on turn 3 Bot1 cannot activate the Viper (no legal target for the ability, CR 601.2c), and the
# Viper stays on the battlefield untapped. The Swamp that would pay {B} is untouched.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Soulcoil Viper
Swamp x2
Swamp x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Memnite
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Soulcoil Viper.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Soulcoil Viper.Activate(Bot2.Graveyard.Memnite)

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Memnite; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield.Soulcoil Viper.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Tapped = false
